course: dictionary
lesson: 14372
title: Words from the orchestra
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orchestral is an adjective. It tells you that something is to do with an orchestra, a large group of musicians playing together. Look for the clue in the word: orchestra plus -al. «The orchestral music filled the concert hall.» The music is played by a whole orchestra, so orchestral means to do with an orchestra.
explain: An orchestra has four families of instruments: strings like the violin, woodwind like the flute, brass like the trumpet, and percussion like the drums. When they all play together, the sound is big and full. That is the kind of sound orchestral describes.
explain: Orchestral can also describe music written for an orchestra, even when you hear it in a film. «The film's orchestral soundtrack made the battle scene feel huge.» Ask yourself: is a whole group of instruments playing? If yes, orchestral probably fits.
fact: Orchestral means to do with an orchestra, or written for an orchestra.
fact: An orchestra is a large group of musicians playing strings, woodwind, brass and percussion together.
fact: «Orchestral music» is music played by an orchestra.
fact: «Orchestral instruments» are the instruments an orchestra uses, such as the violin, flute, trumpet and drums.
fact: An «orchestral version» of a song is the same song arranged for a full orchestra.
exercise: «The orchestral music filled the concert hall.» What does orchestral mean here? | Very quiet and gentle | Made of wood | To do with a football team | *To do with an orchestra
exercise: Which of these is an orchestral instrument? | A kettle | A bicycle | A pencil case | *A violin
exercise: Find the word in «The orchestral music filled the concert hall.» that tells you the music is played by an orchestra. | concert | hall | filled | *orchestral
test: «The film's orchestral soundtrack made the battle scene feel huge.» What does orchestral tell you about the soundtrack? | It was only sung by children | It was played by one person on a phone | It was silent | *It was played by a large group of musicians
test: Which phrase means a piece of music played by a full orchestra? | A muddy field | A cold drink | *An orchestral piece | A paper plane
exam: Which group of instruments is found in an orchestra? | Only drums | Only a piano and a guitar | *Strings, woodwind, brass and percussion | Only the human voice
